# @ts-rest/react-query@3.52.1's peerDependencies for react is "^16.8.0 || ^17.0.0 ||
# ^18.0.0" — it doesn't list 19 yet. This repo runs React 19.2.8 (a pre-existing,
# already-accepted mismatch vs. the documented "React 18" stack — see AGENTS.md and
# ARCHITECTURE.md's decision log; not being silently fixed here).
#
# A root package.json "overrides" entry pinning react/react-dom was tried first and does
# NOT reliably prevent npm from nesting a second, duplicate react copy under
# apps/web/node_modules to satisfy this one peer range — confirmed empirically with a
# from-clean-node_modules install. legacy-peer-deps is the one that actually produces a
# single, deduped react@19.2.8 across the whole tree with no nested copy — verified the
# same way. The trade-off: this relaxes peer-dependency conflict *errors* to warnings
# workspace-wide, not just for this one package — worth knowing before adding a dependency
# with a genuinely incompatible peer range, since npm will no longer refuse the install.
legacy-peer-deps=true
